sign-in-note = Sign in asks Last.fm for a session under the key and secret of an API account you made on last.fm, with the user name and password typed here. The password is sent once and never kept; the session key is kept in the settings file, and what is heard is scrobbled under it within half a minute, beside ListenBrainz where a token is given.
signed-in-note = A Last.fm session is kept: what is heard is scrobbled to Last.fm within half a minute. Signing out forgets the session, not the key and secret.
offline = Last.fm is signed in to only while Online is on
nothing-to-sign-in-with = Give the API key and secret, the user name and the password first
refused = Last.fm refused the sign-in: the user name, the password, or the API key and secret
unreached = Last.fm could not be reached to sign in
signed-out = Nothing heard is scrobbled to Last.fm from now on
the-api-key-of-your-last = The API key of your Last.fm API account, then press enter
its-shared-secret-then-press-enter = Its shared secret, then press enter
your-last-fm-user-name = Your Last.fm user name
your-last-fm-password-then-press = Your Last.fm password, then press enter to sign in
api-key = API key
shared-secret = Shared secret
user-name = User name
password = Password
last-fm-is-not-scrobbled-to = Last.fm is not scrobbled to without its API key and secret
kept-for-signing-in-to-last = Kept for signing in to Last.fm
sign-out-of-last-fm = Sign out of Last.fm
asking-last-fm = Asking Last.fm…
sign-in-to-last-fm = Sign in to Last.fm
signed-in-as = Signed in to Last.fm as { $name } — what is heard from now on is scrobbled there
